# Testing rules for this project (Textile Sourcing/CRM)

When writing or modifying code that touches models, views, serializers,
or services, follow these rules without being asked each time:

1. Every new DRF viewset or queryset MUST filter by `tenant` explicitly.
   Never rely on a default manager to do this silently. If you can't find
   an existing tenant-scoping mixin, ask before inventing a new pattern.

2. Any change to `apps/crm/services/invoicing.py` requires updating
   `tests/unit/test_invoice_logic.py` in the SAME change. Add a new
   parametrize case for any new AgreementType rather than a new test
   function — keep the branches in one table.

3. Any change to `apps/wallet/models.py` (BuyerWallet) requires a test
   proving balance cannot go negative and that `select_for_update` is
   still used in `deduct()`/`credit()`.

4. Use factories from `tests/factories.py` for all test data. Do not
   hand-construct model instances with `Model.objects.create(...)` in
   test files — if a factory is missing a field you need, add it to the
   factory, don't work around it inline.

5. Mark every test with exactly one of: `unit`, `integration`, `tenant`,
   `celery`. Untagged tests will be rejected in review.

6. Do not write a test that only asserts the code does what the code
   currently does. Write the assertion from the spec (BRD/SRS), then
   check it fails before the implementation and passes after.

7. After generating code, run:
   `pytest -m unit -q` for fast feedback, then
   `pytest -m "unit or tenant" -q` before considering the task done.
   Do not report a task as complete without showing the test output.
